  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالسَّمَآءِ وَالطَّارِقِۙ‏(1)\nWAS SAMAAA-E WAT TAAREQE.\nBy the heaven and the Nightly Visitant\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا الطَّارِقُۙ‏(2)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAT-TAAREQUN.\nWhat will let thee know what the Nightly Visitant is?\nالنَّجْمُ الثَّاقِبُۙ‏(3)\nNAJMUS SAAQEBO.\n(It is) the Star of piercing radiance\nاِنْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ لَّمَّا عَلَيْهَا حَافِظٌؕ‏(4)\nIN KULLO NAFSIL LAMMAA A’LAYHAA HAAFEZ.\nThere is not a soul is set a Watcher\nفَلْيَنْظُرِ الْاِنْسَانُ مِمَّ خُلِقَؕ‏(5)\nFAL-YANZORIL INSAANO MIMMA KHOLEQ.\nLet man then reflect, of what he is created\nخُلِقَ مِنْ مَّآءٍ دَافِقٍۙ‏(6)\nKHOLEQA MIM MAAA-IN DAAFEQIN-Y.\nHe is created a water (drop) ejected\nيَّخْرُجُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ الصُّلْبِ وَالتَّرَآئِبِؕ‏(7)\nYAKHROJO MIM BAYNIS SULBE WAT TARAAA-EB.\nComing forth from between the backbone and the ribs\nاِنَّهٗ عَلٰى رَجْعِهٖ لَقَادِرٌؕ‏(8)\nINNAHU A’LAA RAJ-E’HI LA-QAADER.\nVerily, He is Well-Able to resurrect him\nيَوْمَ تُبْلَى السَّرَآئِرُۙ‏(9)\nYAWMA TUBLAS SARAAA-ERO.\nOn the day when all things hidden shall be tried\nفَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ قُوَّةٍ وَّلَا نَاصِرٍؕ‏(10)\nFAMAA LAHU MIN QUWWATINW WA LAA NAASER.\nThen for him shall not be any power, and nor any helper\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الرَّجْعِۙ‏(11)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIR RAJ-E’.\nBy the heaven endued with rotation\nوَالْاَرْضِ ذَاتِ الصَّدْعِۙ‏(12)\nWAL ARZE ZAATIS SAD-E’.\nAnd by the earth endued splitting\nاِنَّهٗ لَقَوْلٌ فَصْلٌۙ‏(13)\nINNAHU LA-QAWLUN FASLUNW.\nVerily, it (the Qur’an) is a decisive word\nوَّمَا هُوَ بِالْهَزْلِؕ‏(14)\nWA MAA HOWA BIL-HAZL.\nAnd it is not a jest\nاِنَّهُمْ يَكِيْدُوْنَ كَيْدًا ۙ‏(15)\nINNAHUM YAKEEDOONA KAYDAANW.\nVerily scheme they (against the truth), a scheme\nوَّاَكِيْدُ كَيْدًا ۚۖ‏(16)\nWA AKEEDO KAYDAA.\nAnd I too do scheme (against them), a scheme\nفَمَهِّلِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَمْهِلْهُمْ رُوَيْدًا‏(17)\nFA-MAH-HELIL KAAFEREENA AMHILHUM ROWAYDAA.\nSo respite thou the disbelievers; let them alone a while",
  "merits": "Surah al-Taariq (The Night-Comer)\nThis Surah has 17 verses and it is a ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is equivalent to ten times the number of heavenly bodies in space.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has narrated that if Surah al-Taariq is recited in compulsory prayers, then the reciter is honoured by Allah (s.w.t.) and will get the opportunity of being with the Prophets (a.s.). Reciting this Surah over anything keeps it safe. If recited before taking medicine, then the medicine will be a sure cure. The water in which this Surah has been dissolved should be poured gently on a wound and it will heal with the Grace of Allah (s.w.t.)."
